# Line endings: normalized to LF in the repository and on checkout.
#
# Windows tooling rewrites files with CRLF, which makes them show as modified
# when nothing changed. In a module repo that churn is worse than cosmetic — it
# makes "the frozen snapshot is untouched" impossible to assert, and it fails
# the freeze gate for a reason that has nothing to do with the data.
#
# DECLARE THIS BEFORE THE FIRST COMMIT. A repository that acquires it later
# needs a renormalization commit that rewrites every line of every text file,
# which buries whatever real change is next to it. Four repos in this estate
# reached production without it and had to be corrected by hand.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: never examined for line endings, never normalized.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.skill binary

# Data binaries. A data module is full of these and the list above was silent
# about them (BF47). `text=auto` already auto-detects every one of them today,
# so this is a declaration and not a remediation -- it says out loud what the
# estate already relies on being inferred. One module carries a committed .db
# and another a .pbix; a 453 KB report normalised as text is not a diff, it is
# a corrupted file.
*.db   binary
*.sqlite binary
*.duckdb binary
*.pbix binary
*.xlsx binary
